Ghost Recon wildlands is out March 7  2017 and we got the chance to explore  Bolivia and Ubisoft Paris's latest  sandbox adventure we played for around 4  hours on the PlayStation 4 Pro and got  to check out two of the games 21 regions  with a game as big as Ghost Recon  wildlands there can be a lot to take in  but here are 7 things you can expect  from the tactical shooter number one  gunsmith and character Smith one of the  coolest things about 2012's Ghost Recon  Future Soldier was the gunsmith gunsmith  allowed you to modify guns to your  heart's content and guess what it's back  with gunsmith you can swap out triggers  stock scopes barrels and just about  everything else in order to make your  own death-dealing frankenstein machine  however in order to unlock new parts for  your guns you'll need to find them  scattered around bolivia i've been  wanting one of these wildlands also  introduces character smith now you can  have your very own frankenstein carrying  around your Frankenstein gun character  Smith was actually pretty robust the  bill didn't have everything unlocked but  there were a lot more options than what  we saw in the division last year number  2 co-op is better in twos while there  may be plenty to do in Bolivia it all  feels kind of empty every mission I took  on in solo my tactics felt kind of  limited by my AI squad but that changes  with a few buddies by your side or maybe  not by your side at all just because  you're in a co-op game doesn't mean you  have to stick with your friends you can  set out and do your own thing or split  up into two groups  better yet whatever you find along the  way is yours to keep  I wouldn't recommend straying too far  from your fellow ghosts though because  sync shot returns and man is it  satisfying it can require some intricate  planning but pulling off a four person  sync shot might be one of the most  satisfying things this game has to offer  she's dead however it seemed like the  ideal way to play wasn't teams of two  coordinating attacks and sync shots were  much easier that way  number three vehicles are plentiful but  kinda sketchy Bolivia is huge  fortunately you won't have to walk  everywhere every single vehicle in the  game is drivable whether that's a plane  helicopter tank or boat you can get in  it you can even drive a backhoe although  I probably wouldn't initiate a frontal  assault in one of these some of these  vehicles can be a bit squirrely at times  and small trees and fences don't always  break as they should however if you  aren't behind the wheel you can still  deploy drones and scout the area and  shoot out the window number four the map  is huge but looks better from a distance  there are 21 different provinces and 11  different ecosystems populated with  herds of llamas flocks of mingos and all  sorts of other wildlife during our  preview we were only able to explore two  of these provinces but there was no  shortage of armed convoys to ambush  helicopters to steal bases to invade  hostages to secure and weapon boxes  define the environments weather effects  and draw distances were also quite  impressive trying to take a base at  night during a thunderstorm is as  exciting as it should be if you don't  have night-vision equipped you'll have  to rely on the headlights of your  vehicle and the quick flashes of  lightning guiding you to your next  destination however the textures up  close were kind of rough but all of  these details created a unique sandbox  with plenty to do and to see number 5  stealth or hit-and-run Ghost Recon  wildlands is still a tactical shooter  and that means you'll need to be smart  making yourself at home in a  fortification will send you back in a  body bag from what we played it seemed  like the best tactics for either stealth  or hit and run if you plan on sneaking  in you probably want to equip a sniper  rifle and pick off the enemies and  watchtowers get rid of AAA turrets and  maybe shoot up the tires on vehicles so  your targets can escape and in case  you're wondering the sniper rifles do  have bullet drops so be wary of that  then it's time to make your approach  sticking to cover and dispatching your  foes silently when  get the chance is key if you don't have  the patience to do that then I'd be  quick plan a route to get in and out  before the enemy calls in too many waves  of reinforcements the longer you spend  in an enemy base the more time backup  has to arrive on the scene if you do  overstay your welcome the AI pushes back  hard the last thing you want are two  helicopters breathing down your neck as  you're trying to make for the hills  fortunately Ghost Recon plays pretty  well it may not feel as smooth as Metal  Gear Solid 5 or Grand Theft Auto 5 but  it certainly gets the job done during  these 10 situations target down  number six the story starts out slow  probably the most uninteresting thing  about Ghost Recon wildlands in the first  few hours is the story the story is  nonlinear meaning that you can complete  missions in any order this is perfect  for co-op play but didn't make me feel  all that invested in the struggles of my  hero or teammates the AI squad mates  were rather annoying at times as well  thanks to some out-of-place dick jokes  and bad dialogue what do you think I'll  swing you was like as a kid probably  pulled the wings off flies burned ants  with a magnifying glass tight cats over  clotheslines maybe he had a cocaine  stand Junior Achievement  maybe he played violent video games that  [ __ ] the video games make people violent  so what makes people violent other  people take a [ __ ] holster  fortunately wildlands does have drop in  and drop out co-op so you shouldn't have  to deal with them for too long  Ghost Recon wildlands is out March 7th  2017 while the build we played did have  some technical issues wildlands is  shaping up to be an exhilarating co-op  experience for more on Tom Clancy's  Ghost Recon wildlands be sure to tune in  to the lobby which now airs on  Wednesdays at 11 a.m. Pacific and if  you're on YouTube make sure to hit that  subscribe button thank you for watching  hey good work in Mong Kok  [Music]
 

